@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.912 = private unnamed_addr constant [496 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of named expressions (e.g., `a := 42`) that can be\0Areplaced by regular assignment statements (e.g., `a = 42`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhile a top-level named expression is syntactically and semantically valid,\0Ait's less clear than a regular assignment statement. Named expressions are\0Aintended to be used in comprehensions and generator expressions, where\0Aassignment statements are not allowed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A(a := 42)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aa = 42\0A```\0A", align 1
