@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.980 = private unnamed_addr constant [730 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for calls of the form `map(int, __version__.split(\22.\22))`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`__version__` does not always contain integral-like elements.\0A\0A```python\0Aimport matplotlib  # `__version__ == \223.9.1.post-1\22` in our environment\0A\0A# ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: 'post1'\0Atuple(map(int, matplotlib.__version__.split(\22.\22)))\0A```\0A\0ASee also [*Version specifiers* | Packaging spec][version-specifier].\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atuple(map(int, matplotlib.__version__.split(\22.\22)))\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport packaging.version as version\0A\0Aversion.parse(matplotlib.__version__)\0A```\0A\0A[version-specifier]: https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/version-specifiers/#version-specifiers\0A", align 1
